0390625, 0.016357421875, -0.0207672119140625, -0.00731658935546875, -0.042236328125, -0.027740478515625, -0.0243682861328125, -0.0400390625, 0.0271148681640625, 0.027435302734375, 0.0159912109375, 0.0175933837890625, 0.00670623779296875, -0.0034694671630859375, 0.01013946533203125, -0.05914306640625, 0.019866943359375, 0.0031032562255859375, 0.0198974609375, 0.034881591796875, -0.037353515625, -0.01189422607421875, -0.0210418701171875, -0.0169830322265625, 0.00011861324310302734, 0.012481689453125, 0.0030269622802734375, 0.020660400390625, 0.01255035400390625, 0.004962921142578125, -0.0002827644348144531, 0.0163726806640625, -0.0031223297119140625, -0.00604248046875, 0.0030918121337890625, 0.013397216796875, 0.01276397705078125, -0.033660888671875, 0.0018701553344726562, -0.005016326904296875, -0.03460693359375, -0.0164337158203125, -0.0012502670288085938, 0.01256561279296875, -0.0282135009765625, 0.01117706298828125, -0.0145263671875, 0.01233673095703125, -0.0018854141235351562, 0.001148223876953125, 0.0006442070007324219, 0.0062408447265625], "payload": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "text": "How level-0 players behave and how they are perceived by higher-level players are central questions in the literature on level-k models of boundedly rational strategic reasoning. To investigate these issues, we use the intra-team communication method developed by Burchardi and Penczynski (2014) to identify level-0 actions and beliefs in both the canonical beauty contest game and a variant of the 11-20 game introduced by Goeree et al. (2018), where observed behavior appears inconsistent with the standard level-k model. In the beauty contest game, we replicate Burchardi and Penczynski\u2019s (2014) finding that elicited level-0 beliefs correspond closely to observed level-0 actions. However, in the variant of the 11-20 game, elicited level-0 beliefs and observed level-0 actions diverge from each other and from the standard level-0 assumption. This divergence suggests a complementary explanation for the behavioral patterns documented by Goeree et al. (2018)."}}